Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_ojpeg.c
Line: 1893
Function: OJPEGReadHeaderInfoSecStreamSof
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: The loop iterates q from 0 to n-1 (where n is derived from the SOF marker length and only checked to equal sp->samples_per_pixel) and writes to sp->sof_c[q], sp->sof_hv[q] (line 1919), and sp->sof_tq[q] (line 1948) without bounding n/sp->samples_per_pixel to the fixed size of these arrays (4, as implied by the 0..3 checks used for JPEG tables earlier). A crafted file with SamplesPerPixel (and SOF Nf) > 4 will cause out-of-bounds writes into the OJPEGState struct.

